---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { ShareGroupMockup } from "../components/ShareGroupMockup";
---

<BaseLayout>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <title>Why this directory exists | Spokane Contractors</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Find a recommended trade. Share their name in one click—no account, no sign-up."
    />
  </Fragment>

  <article class="how-it-works">
    <p class="hero-eyebrow">Why we’re here</p>
    <h1>Find a recommended trade. Share their name in one click.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Need a plumber, electrician, roofer? Stop scrolling messy comment threads.
      This list is for the trades neighbors actually name—and a paste that
      travels complete.
    </p>

    <ShareGroupMockup origin="https://spokanelist.com" />

    <section>
      <h2>No account. No sign-up. No sales spam.</h2>
      <p>
        Search. Find. Share. When you recommend someone, don’t drop a
        half-remembered name. Paste their listing instead. Your neighbor gets
        the number and the site. The contractor gets the call.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>The usual thread</h2>
      <p>
        Someone drops a name from memory. Then the pile-on: what’s their number,
        do they have a site, can I see their Google? You’re hunting instead of
        being helpful. Meanwhile ads show up in the search.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>If you’re the contractor</h2>
      <p>
        Same idea from the other side: a neighbor already dropped your name.
        Let’s make sure they drop your number, too.{" "}
        <a href="/for-contractors">How this works for your business</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="how-actions">
      <a class="button button-primary" href="/">Browse the directory</a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="/how-it-works">How sharing works</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
